# 6. What is a Port?

A **port** is a logical communication endpoint used by network services.

Example:

```text
Server
 |
 ├── Port 22  → SSH
 ├── Port 80  → HTTP
 ├── Port 443 → HTTPS
 └── Port 3389 → RDP
```

Ports range from:

```text
0 – 65535
```

---

# 7. Port Number Categories

| Range | Name |
|---:|---|
| 0–1023 | Well-known/system ports |
| 1024–49151 | Registered ports |
| 49152–65535 | Dynamic/private ports |

