# 37. Nmap Scan Example

Suppose an authorized lab machine is:

```text
192.168.56.101
```

Start with:

```bash
nmap 192.168.56.101
```

Possible result:

```text
PORT     STATE SERVICE
22/tcp   open  ssh
80/tcp   open  http
```

Then perform service detection:

```bash
nmap -sV 192.168.56.101
```

Possible result:

```text
22/tcp   open ssh   OpenSSH ...
80/tcp   open http  Apache ...
```

Then, if permitted:

```bash
nmap -sC 192.168.56.101
```

This adds default NSE-based enumeration.

